ge transformations to handle skewness, create deeper feature interactions for complex relationships, and streamline the feature set by eliminating noise from uninformative features. This balanced approach enhances both the interpretability and effectiveness of the downstream classification model.', "```python\n# log_F03[C-O]\n# Feature description: Logarithmic transformation of F03[C-O] (frequency of C-O bonds at topological distance 3).\n# Usefulness: F03[C-O] is highly skewed (mean = 3.6524, median = 2.0, Q3 = 6.0). Applying a log transformation reduces the effect of outliers and normalizes the data, making it more suitable for downstream tasks.\ndf['log_F03[C-O]'] = np.log1p(df['F03[C-O]'])\n```end\n\n```python\n# carbon_to_oxygen_ratio\n# Feature description: Ratio of C% (percentage of carbon atoms) to nO (number of oxygen atoms).\n# Usefulness: This ratio highlights the balance between carbon content and oxygen atoms, which is critical for understanding the molecular structure's biodegradability. Oxygen is often associated with functional groups important for biodegradation.\ndf['carbon_to_oxygen_ratio'] = df['C%'] / (df['nO'] + 1e-6)  # Adding 1e-6 to avoid division by zero\n```end\n\n```python\n# interaction_SM6_L_TI2_L\n# Feature description: Multiplication of SM6_L (spectral moment of order 6 from Laplace matrix) and TI2_L (second Mohar index from Laplace matrix).\n# Usefulness: Combining these graph-based features captures molecular structural complexity and connectivity, which are key factors influencing chemical activity and biodegradability.\ndf['interaction_SM6_L_TI2_L'] = df['SM6_L'] * df['TI2_L']\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column B01[C-Br] is dropped\n# The feature B01[C-Br] (presence/absence of C-Br at topological distance 1) has very low variance (mean = 0.0442, std = 0.2058), with most values being zero. It provides limited information and adds noise to the model.\ndf.drop(columns=['B01[C-Br]'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\